Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:08:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 127/154] fix(peek): Cmd+Shift+click on a link opens a focused
 tab, not a peek
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Cmd+Shift+click and a noopener link both reach Browser::OpenURLFromTab
as NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB with nothing in the params to tell them apart, so
the off-site rule for a favourite's tab turned the click into a peek.
The click's modifiers are still held when its IPC lands, so the branch
now reads them and lets the accelerator through to a foreground tab.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
index 29df7e61e460b..484a364276a53 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
@@ -293,6 +293,7 @@
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_feature_check.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_new_tab_modifiers.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_peek_intercept.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_status_bubble_hook.h"
 #include "ui/display/display.h"
@@ -1551,10 +1552,11 @@ WebContents* Browser::OpenURLFromTab(
   }
   // Auto-peek for a plain click lives in AtriumPeekNavigationThrottle, since
   // a plain click emits no OpenURL IPC. A window.open with noopener does,
-  // as NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB, so the same off-site rule applies here.
+  // as NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB, so the same off-site rule applies here. So does a
+  // Cmd+Shift+click, which asked for a focused tab.
   if (params.disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB &&
       params.is_renderer_initiated && params.user_gesture &&
-      !params.started_from_context_menu &&
+      !params.started_from_context_menu && !atrium::NewTabModifiersHeld() &&
       atrium::ShouldAutoPeek(this, source, params.url) &&
       atrium::MaybeOpenPeek(this, source, params.url, params.referrer)) {
     return source;
